Z||000003||MikeSchaefer||02-15-2001||11:36 AM||||Hi Phil,<BR>Beautiful car, I have a question for you;  When you mounted the stands to the wing, what did you use?  I remember the first wing I did, I just glassed it, that lasted about 3 months then it started to come apart.  Then the second time I rivited it on and used a special plastic to fiberglass epoxy to hold it, which seemed to work well but I always felt like there was another way to do it.  Now I have another spoiler with some stainless steel mounts (fiberglass filled), and will be putting it together soon.  What do you think would be the best approach?<BR>Thanks a million,<BR>Mike Schaefer <A HREF="http://surf.to/fiero" TARGET=_blank>http://surf.to/fiero</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Phil||02-15-2001||01:04 PM||||<BR>Thanks guys <BR>For the wing, I just screwed it on like the originals. <BR>The tail lights are from Pisa and the sequential system  is a modified Larry Mazza(sp) design||||reg||1
Z||000005||stsmithgt||02-15-2001||01:11 PM||||It looks like the factory screws.  I sure like those taller stands.  My hands don't fit  under the wing very well to clean and shine it up.  I'd like to get, or if I have to, make some taller ones for mine.  Hmm? You use super glue and Lego's right?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>And on that note:  I'm getting my car back from the Fiero Shop today! <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/smiley_dance.gif"> <p>[This message has been edited by stsmithgt (edited 02-15-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||Phil||02-15-2001||02:31 PM||||One modification I forgot to mention: I lowered my inside mirror about 2"  so that I can easily look out under the wing.||||reg||1
